Here's what I try to obtain for a truly powerful character.

Two weapons...  As a Valkyrie I usually end up with Excalibur and
Longsword and then switch out Excalibur for Mjollnir on the astral
plane.  Unless of course I get Grayswandir or something to that
effect... that trumps both Excalibur and Mjollnir.  Although Mjollnir
is usefull on the plane of air because you can throw it at enemies, it
comes back to you, and you move a square in the opposite direction(if
you're levitating).  This allows you to attack Air Elementals at the
same time as fleeing from them.

Blessed Amulet of Life Saving (Whenever I'm not using ESP)
Blessed Amulet of ESP (when I need it)
Blessed Ring of Polymorph (Just keep turning into an Aleax... they can
dual wield, wear all armor, have more AC, and get an extra kick
attack)
Blessed Ring of Slow Digestion(When Im not using something else on my
second finger)
Blessed Ring of Levitation (for special scenarios.. medusa's island,
plane of air, plane of water, etc...)
Blessed Ring of Conflict
Blessed Greased Silver Dragon Scale Mail
Blessed Fireproof Speed boots
Blessed Rustproof Helm of Brilliance
Blessed Fireproof Cloak of Magic Resistance
Blessed Fireproof T-Shirt
Blessed Rustproof Gauntlets of Power

This setup is caster friendly except for the gauntlets of power but
those are trivial to remove for a turn or 2.  As a Valkyrie, attack
spells aren't going to be a main source of damage for you so there is
rarely a need for a spell-casting Valkyrie to actually remove the
gauntlets during combat.  Although, if you really want to be
spellcaster friendly, replace the gauntlets of power with gauntlets of
dexterity.

To answer your question more directly... I use "oLS almost 100% of the
time once I have it.  Exceptions come on a case by case basis... but
its almost never necessary to wear the ESP for an extended period of
time. Put it on once every time you enter a new level and maybe
periodically while exploring for a turn or two.  Now, do I need the
"oLS? Absolutely not.  I can(and have) ascended without one... but why
play without that extra buffer of protection unless you have to?
Although, I do not think it is worth a wish.  Not unless you really
really think you're going to need it.  Or if you've already used the
guaranteed one and are about to go on the astral plane(or plane of
air) without one. There's a guaranteed "oLS every game.

Of course, this is just all my opinion on how to make a really pimp
Valkyrie and there's some things missing( a couple rings, wands,
special tools, etc...), but it definitely seems to pwn just as much as
any other ascension kit combo I've seen.  I mean, really at that point
it doesn't matter much. As long as you have all the intrinsics/
extrinsics you need and have at least -25 AC  most of the rest of the
game is a cakewalk.  I just like that particular combo of equipment
because I can throw Mjollnir and have it return, I can dual wield, and
I have all the intrinsics/extrinsics that are generally considered
necessities


